## Root Cause Analysis (5 Whys)

1. **Why did users experience 502 Bad Gateway errors?**
   The authentication service crashed in a continuous restart loop.
2. **Why was the service crashing?**
   An unhandled null pointer occurred during startup when parsing JWT signing keys.
3. **Why was the signing key null?**
   The release configuration omitted a required environment variable key name change.
4. **Why was this not caught in staging?**
   Staging environment had a fallback mock key configured directly in the deployment YAML.
5. **Why was staging config drift allowed?**
   Staging and production deployment manifests were maintained in separate, non-templated files.

## What Went Well

- Automated alerting notified on-call within 2 minutes of the regression.
- Fast rollback command restored customer traffic in under 15 minutes from triage.

## Where We Got Lucky

- Outage occurred during a scheduled maintenance window with reduced traffic volume.

